  "published": "2026-11-19T21:40:46.43Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Observations, Lists, SNOMED codes and the patient's telecom now match what DDS sends.\n\t\t  - Every Observation carries the vital-signs category, as DDS sends it, and its date goes out as effectivePeriod.start instead of effectiveDateTime.\n\t\t  - Every List carries a date: the time the record was built, in UTC to the second, the same on every List in the record. The Miscellaneous record list still sorts by the Observation's period start.\n\t\t  - SNOMED codes the mart labels snomed_info_sct or http:__snomed.info_sct now get a SNOMED coding in all eight mappers that read a code category. The labels are a new setting, OtherSnomedCodeCategories on FhirIdentifierConfigurations, with those two as the default; SnomedCodeCategory is unchanged.\n\t\t  - An Observation with a SNOMED code but no description now sends the coding without a display, instead of dropping the code.\n\t\t  - The patient's home phone goes out as the first telecom (phone, home), ahead of email and mobile, as in DDS. A blank home phone is left off.\n\t\t  - New IDateTimeBroker, registered by both the client and AddOlidsToFhirMapperServices. No consumer change is needed.",
